---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'what-season-0-is',
    label: '01 / Setup Phase',
    title: 'What Season 0 Is',
  },
  {
    id: 'how-survival-should-feel',
    label: '02 / Design Intent',
    title: 'How DeadMTL Survival Should Feel',
  },
  {
    id: 'enclave-doctrine',
    label: '03 / First Sector',
    title: 'First Enclave Doctrine',
  },
  {
    id: 'player-principles',
    label: '04 / Field Rules',
    title: 'Player Principles',
  },
  {
    id: 'human-behind-player',
    label: '05 / Network Layer',
    title: 'The Human Behind the Player',
  },
  {
    id: 'current-limits',
    label: '06 / Honest Limits',
    title: 'Current Limits',
  },
] as const;
---

<Base
  title="Season 0 Survival Primer"
  description="DeadMTL Season 0 Survival Primer — survival design intent, first enclave doctrine, player principles, and current server limits."
>

<!-- ─── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="term-hero" style="padding-block: clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem);">
  <div class="th__inner">
    <div class="th__eyebrow">SURVIVAL GUIDE // KNOWLEDGE CENTER // SEASON 0</div>
    <div class="th__headline" style="font-size: clamp(1.6rem,4.5vw,3rem);">Season 0 Survival Primer</div>
    <p class="th__body">
      What DeadMTL survival means, how the first enclave works, and what a player should know before connecting.
      The server is not open yet. This article is preparation, not connection instructions.
    </p>
    <div class="th__cta">
      <a href="#what-season-0-is"        class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">Start Reading &rsaquo;</a>
      <a href="/knowledge/"              class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">&larr; Knowledge Center</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── SECTION NAV ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" style="padding-block: 1.5rem;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="term-panel">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Document Index</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">6 sections</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding: 0.75rem 0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0;">
        {sections.map(s => (
          <a
            href={`#${s.id}`}
            style="padding:0.55rem 1.25rem; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.72rem; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:var(--text-dim); border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-subtle); display:flex; gap:1.5rem; text-decoration:none; transition:background 0.12s, color 0.12s;"
            onmouseover="this.style.background='var(--graphite)'; this.style.color='var(--cream)';"
            onmouseout="this.style.background=''; this.style.color='var(--text-dim)';"
          >
            <span style="color:var(--text-muted); flex-shrink:0;">{s.label}</span>
            <span>{s.title}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 01: WHAT SEASON 0 IS ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="what-season-0-is">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">01 / Setup Phase</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">What Season 0 Is</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel term-panel--amber" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag th__tag--amber">Status Check</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">Server Pending</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem 1.25rem; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.78rem; color:var(--amber); line-height:1.65;">
        Server is not open. Whitelist is closed. No connection details. No launch date.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        Season 0 is the first test season of DeadMTL. It is a setup phase, not a full launch.
        The map is being built. The server infrastructure is being prepared. The rules are being finalized.
        The modlist has not been locked.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first playable philosophy is containment. One sector. One enclave.
        Saint-Paul-&Eacute;mard. The game does not start with the whole city. It starts with the
        piece of the city that is still manageable. Everything else is pressure from outside.
      </p>
      <p>
        Season 0 players are early participants in a test run. Expect configuration changes,
        possible wipes, rule revisions, and map updates during this phase. Stability comes later.
        Season 0 is proof-of-concept, not the finished product.
      </p>
      <p>
        When Season 0 opens, it will be announced on this site and through the dispatch channel.
        Until that announcement appears here, the server is not accepting connections.
        There are no valid server addresses being shared anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 02: HOW SURVIVAL SHOULD FEEL ────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="how-survival-should-feel">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">02 / Design Intent</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">How DeadMTL Survival Should Feel</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        DeadMTL is not a server for grinding resources in safety. The design intent is a
        world where survival choices have real cost.
      </p>

      <h2>Movement matters.</h2>
      <p>
        Where you go, how fast you move, whether you run or walk, whether you cut through
        an alley or take the longer road — these are decisions with consequences. Noise
        draws attention. Speed sacrifices situational awareness. Every route through the
        enclave has known and unknown risks.
      </p>

      <h2>Scarcity matters.</h2>
      <p>
        Resources in a post-collapse Montreal neighbourhood are finite and distributed unevenly.
        Early access to a location does not guarantee it stays useful. Other players deplete
        supplies. Events change availability. Carrying everything you find is not a strategy.
        Carrying what you need and leaving the rest for others — or for later — is.
      </p>

      <h2>Information matters.</h2>
      <p>
        The dispatch channel, zone dossiers, and knowledge center exist because information
        about the enclave has value. Which areas are hot. Where the gates are. What the
        Jolicoeur Barrier situation looks like. A player who reads the network before entering
        a sector makes better decisions than one who does not.
      </p>

      <h2>Noise matters.</h2>
      <p>
        Project Zomboid's noise and attention mechanics are the backbone of this server's
        survival style. Generators are a liability as much as an asset. Gunshots are
        announcement. Loud entry techniques have persistent consequences.
      </p>

      <h2>Weather and darkness matter.</h2>
      <p>
        Montreal winter conditions affect movement, visibility, and resource access.
        The enclave is set in winter 1993&ndash;1994. Cold, snow, darkness, and fog are
        not atmosphere. They are environmental pressure.
      </p>

      <h2>Small group trust matters.</h2>
      <p>
        DeadMTL is a whitelist server. The player pool is small and curated. A server
        where everyone is a stranger creates a different social contract than a public
        open-door server. Trust is earned by behaviour, not by default.
        Communication, honesty about resource locations, and backing up other players
        under pressure are the survival layer that no rule can fully enforce.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 03: FIRST ENCLAVE DOCTRINE ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="enclave-doctrine">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">03 / First Sector</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">First Enclave Doctrine</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        Saint-Paul-&Eacute;mard is the first active sector. It is not a safe zone.
        It is the sector that is still manageable enough to be the starting point.
        That distinction matters.
      </p>
      <p>
        The enclave combines Ville-&Eacute;mard and C&ocirc;te-Saint-Paul into a single
        DeadMTL sector identity. It is enclosed by the canal to the north and the pressure
        fronts to the south and west. The borders are not walls. They are lines where the
        threat increases sharply.
      </p>

      <h2>Canal edge pressure.</h2>
      <p>
        The Canal de Lachine forms the northern boundary. Crossing it reaches Saint-Henri,
        which is not in Season 0 scope. The canal edge is an industrial route — workshops,
        waterline fog, uneven movement risk. It is active but not safe.
      </p>

      <h2>LaSalle pressure front.</h2>
      <p>
        LaSalle is the primary threat source from the south and west. The Pont Mercier
        barricade failure is the origin of the largest horde pressure in the southwest.
        LaSalle is not a playable zone. It is the reason the enclave cannot expand southwest
        without consequences.
      </p>

      <h2>No fake total-city claim.</h2>
      <p>
        DeadMTL is not claiming to map all of Montreal. Season 0 covers one sector.
        The map section of this site lists planning labels for future expansion, but those
        are planning labels, not promises. The enclave is the game. Everything outside it
        is context and pressure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 04: PLAYER PRINCIPLES ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="player-principles">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">04 / Field Rules</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">Player Principles</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Field Doctrine</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0;">
        {[
          ['Scout before looting', 'Know what is in a building and what is around it before committing to entry.'],
          ['Carry less than you want', 'Weight affects movement. Movement affects survival. Prioritise what you need, not what you found.'],
          ['Never assume roads are safe', 'A road clear yesterday may not be clear now. Movement history does not guarantee current state.'],
          ['Mark routes', 'If you find a safe path, note it. If a path changes, update that note. The map is shared information.'],
          ['Read dispatches', 'The dispatch channel carries real information about sector events. It is not decoration.'],
          ['Respect server rules', 'The rules exist because the server is a shared resource. Enforcement is not the point. Behaviour is.'],
          ['No power fantasy', 'DeadMTL is not designed for optimised speedruns or resource dominance. It is designed for survival.'],
        ].map(([principle, desc]) => (
          <div style="padding:0.75rem 1.25rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.78rem; color:var(--bone); margin-bottom:0.25rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.04em;">{principle}</div>
            <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.72rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.55;">{desc}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 05: HUMAN BEHIND THE PLAYER ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="human-behind-player">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">05 / Network Layer</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">The Human Behind the Player</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        Project Zomboid is played by a character. The character survives or does not.
        But the human behind the character exists outside the game, and that human
        has access to the DeadMTL network.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Knowledge Center, dispatch channel, map section, and rules are not in-game resources.
        They exist for the human reading the screen. The player navigates the enclave.
        The human reads the context.
      </p>
      <p>
        This distinction matters because some of what DeadMTL does is out-of-world.
        Operator notes explain what is happening with the project. Server notices explain
        what is happening with the server. Field reports and network dispatches are in-world
        fiction. The dispatch taxonomy page explains which is which.
      </p>
      <p>
        A player who understands how the enclave works, what the pressure zones are,
        what the rules say, and what kind of server this is before logging in will have
        a better experience than one who connects blind. The network exists to support that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── 06: CURRENT LIMITS ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" id="current-limits">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">06 / Honest Limits</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">Current Limits</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        DeadMTL is in setup. These are the current limits, stated plainly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-feed" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      {[
        ['Server',         'Pending. Not running. No connection address has been published.'],
        ['Whitelist',      'Closed. Applications are not open. No approval process is active.'],
        ['Map',            'Under construction. Sector names are planning labels. PZMapForge tooling is active but the map is not final.'],
        ['Metro / Tunnel', 'Concept only. Not in Season 0 scope. The Dead Line is a future layer, not a current one.'],
        ['Modlist',        'Not finalized. The required mod list has not been published. Do not subscribe to mods based on guessing.'],
        ['Discord',        'No server exists yet. No invite will be shared until one is created and linked here.'],
        ['Launch Date',    'None. There is no announced launch date. When Season 0 opens, this site will say so.'],
      ].map(([label, status]) => (
        <div class="feed-item">
          <span class="fi__type fi__type--system">{label}</span>
          <div class="fi__body">
            <p class="fi__text">{status}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="dispatch-entry">
      <p>
        Content on this site may change before launch. Sector names, rules, survival guides,
        and modlist are all provisional until Season 0 opens. The site is built in public
        because transparency is part of the project's design philosophy.
        Everything here reflects the actual state of the project at the time it was written.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── FOOTER CTA ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="home-section" style="padding-block:2.5rem;">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="display:flex; gap:0.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="/rules/"      class="term-btn term-btn--teal">Read Rules &rsaquo;</a>
      <a href="/map/"        class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">Open Map &rsaquo;</a>
      <a href="/dispatch/"   class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">Dispatches &rsaquo;</a>
      <a href="/knowledge/"  class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">&larr; Knowledge Center</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
